---
title: Icteridae
---
# Icteridae

Icteridae is the New World blackbird family, which takes in the grackles, the
cowbirds, the meadowlarks and the American orioles. The bill is conical and
sharply pointed, and the family feeds by gaping: the closed bill is driven into
turf or a curled leaf and then forced open, prising the substrate apart. Habits
vary enormously across the family, from colonial cowbirds that lay in the
clutches of other species to orioles that suspend a deep plaited pouch from a
branch tip. See [[baltimore-oriole]].
